  "details": "I don't like to say it but vr chat lives partly through the mods. Personally, I rarely use them and have often played without mods, but there are others who sometimes consider mods necessary. I looked at a game which is very mod friendly and has a well working system: Beamng drive. There you can download the mods in the game yourself. Anyone can send their mods to Beamng drive, they will then be checked and released accordingly or not released. I think such a system would be very close to the community and would make many people happy despite the anti-cheat. I don't know exactly if it's that easy, but I believe in the Vrchat team that it can implement something like that. Of course, I also know that resources would have to be turned off for the mod review and that may be difficult to implement. However, such a feature would make me very happy. IMPORTANT: VR chat must, however, state that mods may not work with others and that they are not responsible for protecting themselves and making it clear that if there are problems, the mod creator must be contacted not the vr chat support",
